  "description": "Engine health read from its own logs: what the broom had to correct, whether that means a defect elsewhere, and whether its passes keep up.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "liveNow": false,
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "The broom is the engine's only periodic reconciler for the running half of the domain lifecycle. **It correcting a row means something else failed to converge it** \u2014 seven of its eight corrections are classified `upstream_failure` and logged at WARNING; only a guest ignoring ACPI (`force_stop_after_shutdown_timeout`) is `expected`.\n\nA quiet installation shows **zero** on the first three panels. Anything above zero on *Corrections that mean a defect* is a bug to chase, not routine housekeeping.\n\n---\n\n**Why the queries filter on `\"msg\":`.** The engine emits every log line **three times** \u2014 two text handlers and a JSON one \u2014 so an unfiltered `|= \"BROOM_ACTED\"` counts each correction three times. Selecting the JSON emission gives the real number. Measured on a staging install: 9 unfiltered against 3 real."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Broom corrections",
      "description": "Every corrective write the broom made in the selected range. Zero is the healthy value.",
      "id": 2,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "P8E80F9AEF21F6940"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "P8E80F9AEF21F6940"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({container_name=\"isard-engine\", domain=~\"$install\"} |= \"\\\"msg\\\": \\\"BROOM_ACTED\" [$__range]))",
          "queryType": "instant",
